! TightOPT PBE0 D3BJ RIJCOSX def2-TZVP def2/J CPCM(water)

# Hydrogen-only optimization, deliberately with NO "! AnFreq".
#
# Heavy atoms stay at their carved (crystallographic) positions; only the protons
# move. That is the point of this mode: hydrogens in a carved PDB cluster are
# added by a protonation step rather than observed, and their positions are what
# FEFF's muffin-tin construction trips over. Every muffin-tin overlap failure
# surveyed in 4cys/first-set was a heavy-atom---H pair (12x C---H, 2x S---H,
# never heavy---heavy), so relaxing the protons targets exactly the atoms
# responsible while leaving the heavy-atom skeleton untouched.
#
# The Hessian is NOT computed here. It is interpolated from the packaged ligand
# spring models by xas_pipeline.stages.interp_hessian, which the corvus wrapper
# runs before prepare-corvus and which writes the same <run_id>.hess the
# CORVUS/FEFF stage expects. Adding "! AnFreq" back would spend the
# analytic-frequency time this mode exists to avoid AND have its .hess
# immediately overwritten by the interpolated one -- do not "fix" its absence.

! 6-311++G(d,p)
! ZORA ZORA-def2-TZVP SARC/J

%basis
  NewGTO Zn "def2-TZVPP" end
end

# Per-process memory in MB, sized by prepare-orca.py from the atom count
%maxcore [MAXCORE]

# Specify numnber of processors
%pal nprocs 16
  end

# Only optimize H atom locations
%geom
 optimizehydrogens true
end

# Use xyz file, first number is charge, second number is multiplicity (2S+1)
*xyzfile [CHARGE] [MULTIPLICITY] [ID_DIR]/[PDB_ID]_clean.xyz
